END_IF;

//==============================================================================
// NOTES AND BEST PRACTICES
//==============================================================================
//
// 1. Work Time Tracking:
//    - Update work times continuously when devices are running
//    - Store work times in persistent (RETAIN) memory to survive power cycles
//    - Use separate timer logic to accumulate runtime into the WorkTime structure
//
// 2. Ready Signal:
//    - Connect to device feedback: running status, no faults, available
//    - Include permissive conditions: not in maintenance, not failed
//
// 3. Toggle Signal:
//    - Can use General_FB pulses for automatic rotation
//    - Can use operator button for manual rotation
//    - Can use process conditions (shift change, daily reset, etc.)
//
// 4. Number of Devices to Run:
//    - Can be constant or variable based on demand
//    - Should be validated (0-10 range)
//    - Can be changed dynamically during operation
//
// 5. Monitoring:
//    - Always monitor InsufficientDevices flag
//    - Log toggle events for maintenance tracking
//    - Track total runtime for maintenance scheduling
//
// 6. Testing:
//    - Test with various combinations of ready devices
//    - Test toggle functionality
//    - Test with NumberOfDevicesToRun = 0 and = 10
//    - Test with unequal work times
//    - Verify priority: Ready > WorkTime > Device Number
//
//==============================================================================
